UID:10015046-1792836000-1792843200@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:RegenAll + PCA&D: Love Letters to Tomorrow: Collage Workshop: Grades 4-6
DESCRIPTION:In 2026\, RegenAll’s Youth Climate Art Exhibition will be a pre-event component of RegenAll’s Annual Climate Summit. Students from around the county will have the opportunity to express their vision of a thriving\, resilient\, and sustainable “green future” to promote creative and hopeful thinking for the next generation. We hope that their work will inspire decision-makers\, lawmakers\, and community members to see a better future for our shared environment. The exhibition will be held November 8 – 15 at Pennsylvania College of Art & Design’s Welcome Center (241 N. Prince Street\, Lancaster\, PA ) with an opening reception on Friday\, November 13\, 2026 from 5 – 7:30 pm.  \n\n\n\nOne way for young community members to submit work is in one of our free workshops held at PCA&D! Join us! There are endless ways to find and use our creative voices to uplift and advocate for things important to us! In this workshop\, students in grades 4-6 will learn more about how poetry can communicate our values by using found objects and magazines to write their own blackout poem. Together\, we’ll explore examples of collage poems and discuss how to reuse materials to create something new before writing and collaging our own!  \n\n\n\nInstructor: Sam Sweigert  \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/regenall-pcad-love-letters-to-tomorrow-collage-workshop-grades-4-6/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/3.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
