LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T202543Z
UID:10015002-1792836000-1792846800@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:Sugar Skull Mosaic Workshop at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, you will make a 7-inch sugar skull mosaic. You will learn how to cut glass pieces into different sizes and shapes with hand tools\, then layout and attach those pieces. We will finish the mosaics with grouting. Let’s celebrate Day of the Dead with your hand-made sugar skull mosaics! All materials are provided for this class. This class is primarily studio based. You will start with a brief lecture and spend most of the class creating with guidance from your instructor.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: You will be working with sharp glass and nipping tools. This class requires careful listening and abiding by appropriate safety procedures. Please dress accordingly. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/sugar-skull-mosaic-workshop-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/Sugar-Skull-Mosaic-Workshop.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
