SUMMARY:Beginning Portrait Painting Workshop at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:In this live portrait painting workshop\, students will gain the skills of building up likeness working simple to complex\, building confidence in their palette choices\, design choices\, and anatomical knowledge. Working in the painting medium of their choice\, students will sit through a demonstration of how to begin\, clarify and resolve a portrait painting while working on their own and integrating the lesson first hand. Color theory\, color fields of the face\, structure\, anatomy\, and design will all be covered. Note: Students provide their own materials. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/beginning-portrait-painting-workshop-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/portrait-workshop.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
