SUMMARY:Family History: Tall Tales and Folklore at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:What’s your go-to fireside story? What about that family tale that’s so extraordinary that it’s unbelievable? In this workshop\, we’ll hone our narrative craft (including setting\, character\, and description) as we flesh out the stories we grew up hearing\, telling\, and passing along! Students in this course will read and respond to a sample text\, draft their own heirloom story\, and receive feedback from peers and instructor. While there won’t be a literal campfire\, we’ll spend the evening spinning yarns. After all\, everyone’s got a story to tell! This is a lecture based and creative writing class with some lecture and guidance followed by time to write using the skills learned in class. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/family-history-tall-tales-and-folklore-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/LifeWriting.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
