SUMMARY:White House Workers
DESCRIPTION:Join White House Historical Association historian Sarah Fling as she highlights lesser-known stories of White House workers throughout history\, including the men and women who worked for President James Buchanan.  \n\n\n\nSarah Fling is a historian at the White House Historical Association. Her research focuses on free and enslaved workers\, the first ladies\, and the White House Collection. Fling is a contributor in The Cambridge Companion to US First Ladies (2025) and has published her research in White House History Quarterly and Teen Vogue. She serves on the Board of the Smithsonian’s National Museum of American History\, and previously served as a Community Lead in the Youth250 Bureau\, a non-partisan initiative that highlighted the Gen Z perspective during America’s 250th. Sarah’s previous work experience includes internships at historic sites such as George Washington’s Mount Vernon and the Frick Pittsburgh. She received her bachelor’s degree in History from the University of Pittsburgh and her master’s in Public History from American University.  \n\n\n\nDoors open and the reception begins at 5pm. The lecture will begin at 5:30pm. The lecture will also be streamed to Zoom at 5:30pm for those who wish to join us virtually. This program is free and open to the public. In-person attendance requires advance registration in order to guarantee a seat. Due to capacity restrictions\, tickets may not be available at the door. Virtual attendance requires advance registration in order to receive the Zoom link. Register online by clicking the appropriate link below or by calling 717.392.4633. The online version of this program will also be recorded and uploaded to LancasterHistory’s YouTube channel after the event. \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/white-house-workers/
LOCATION:LancasterHistory\, 230 North President Ave\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/10/Sarah-Fling.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="LancasterHistory":MAILTO:info@lancasterhistory.org
END:VEVENT
